                      "id": "buZDf",
                      "name": "State note",
                      "fill": "$subtle",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Every build starts the embedded MCP server on 127.0.0.1 with a port the OS picks; the item shows that address in Geist Mono $subtle, between the right separator and the version, with or without a project. It opens nothing (pointer only, no focus): the endpoint alone does not let a client in. Its hint, like every status bar hint, hangs 6 px above the bar on $raised and stays inside the window (here flush with its right edge); it names the endpoint and says clients read the access token from this process's discovery file. The token itself is never shown, copied or logged.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
