                      "id": "sJV5E",
                      "name": "State note",
                      "fill": "$subtle",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The plan limits item (hourglass) sits right after Tokens today, before the right separator. One entry per agent CLI that this project’s connections use: the CLI name in $muted and the used share of its fullest window in Geist Mono $text (Codex 12% and 65% → 65%). The numbers arrive with agent turns: Codex rate_limits (used_percent, window_minutes, resets_at, plan_type, credits) and Claude Code rate_limit_event (rateLimitType, utilization, resetsAt, status). The hint, in the status bar hint style (360 wide here, padding 8, gap 8), lists each window with a 100 × 4 meter ($border track, $muted fill), its reset (relative under 24 h, weekday and time beyond), and where the numbers came from and when. A window a CLI has not reported since the app started reads Not reported yet. Pointer only, no focus, no click target.",
