                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "aRknn",
                      "name": "State note",
                      "fill": "$subtle",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A limit is reached when the CLI says so (Codex rate_limit_reached_type set, Claude Code status rejected) or a window reads 100%. The item takes the emphasis the status bar already uses for something that blocks work (states H and I): a $raised fill, octagon-pause (the Stopped at limit icon) in $text, and the reset time in place of the percentage: Codex limit reached · resets 16:40 (weekday and time when the reset is a day or more away, resets Mon 09:00). The other CLI keeps its compact entry. The hint names the full window and says what the CLI does: Codex refuses new turns until 16:40. Orchester adds no run behaviour: a run whose agent hit the limit ends the way it does today (its task shows the stop or failure and the CLI message); the item only tells, from every screen, when work can start again. At the reset time the number is no longer known: the item shows Codex — and the hint Reset at 16:40 · read again with the next Codex turn, until a turn reports again. No colour: $danger stays reserved for Unreadable.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
