                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "QrNYr",
                      "name": "State note",
                      "fill": "$subtle",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "No working connection: the project has a connection for the CLI but its last check could not start it (not found, did not answer); the hint names the connection and the check time and points to Connections. After a reset: the reset time has passed, so the used share is unknown until a turn reports again; the row keeps the window, drops the meter and says Reset at 16:40 · read again with the next turn, and the compact entry becomes a dash. Credits (Codex credits.has_credits; balance as reported, unit unverified; unlimited reads Unlimited) and extra usage (Claude Code isUsingOverage) are rows under the windows, shown only when the CLI reports them. With extra usage in use a full window does not block turns, so it gets the near-limit emphasis, not the reached one.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
