                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "The traffic lights stay where macOS puts them (12px from the edge, 8 apart) inside the 216 area over the sidebar; the tabs start at 216 like on Windows, so they never move between platforms or pages. Everything right of + is drag area up to the window edge. In full screen the traffic lights hide and the area stays empty. Shortcuts use Cmd (Cmd+T, Cmd+W, Cmd+1…9); Ctrl+Tab still switches tabs.",
